  "claimBoundary": "Frozen synthetic campaigns, criterion on reversible decisions only. The named method under test (a ladder requiring two signals to agree) cleared the 25% effect floor in 1 of 8 powered cells and the criterion is rejected. Bait, a reported arm, cleared it in 8 of 8 (34-77%) with no harm flags, but declaring it the answer now would be choosing after seeing outcomes; a successor must name it in advance. Reflection cleared the floor while making 6,497-8,782 false merges per cell, which is why prevention without a harm test is not a measure of a detector. No real-world rates; probing assumes a touchable upstream; irreversible decisions out of scope; same control domain; no authority claim."
